From: Ovidijus Vyšniauskas (ovid-io)
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd-clsh: run the v3 class-H start-up only for the first headphone channel

wcd_clsh_v3_state_hph_l() and _hph_r() force the start-up IQ settings
(FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2[7:5] 0xa0, CLASSH_MODE_3 bit 1, CLASSH_MODE_2
0x1c), then enable flyback and buck, whose first user restores the
playback values (0xe0, bit 1 clear, 0x3a). For the second channel
flyback and buck are already on, so their restore is skipped and the
start-up values forced again stay: measured on a KONKR Pocket FIT
(WCD9395) playing in CLS_H_ULP, CLASSH_MODE_2 0x1c, CLASSH_MODE_3 0xf2,
FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2 0xb8, where stock Android has 0x3a, 0xf0, 0xf8.
With the supply left in its start-up state, loud passages clip at about
three quarters of full volume, or drop out briefly with the compander
on, while Android plays the same track clean and louder.

Qualcomm's downstream state machine calls the stereo state's handler
when the second channel joins, which does nothing, so the sequence runs
once. Do the same here: force the start-up settings only when neither
buck nor flyback is on yet.

The repeated start-up was found by mrdidit on the AYANEO Pocket S2.
Tested on a KONKR Pocket FIT on Armada 20261109 (this patch built as the
module against its kernel): the three registers read 0x3a, 0xf0, 0xf8
while playing, and with the class-H port fix (0082) headphones play
clean at full volume in ULP with the compander on, as on Android.

This is wcd-clsh-v2's v3 path, shared by WCD937x, WCD938x and WCD939x.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
index 62ca22e..c022a04 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
@@ -547,7 +547,15 @@ static void wcd_clsh_v3_state_hph_r(struct wcd_clsh_ctrl *ctrl, int req_state,
 	if (is_enable) {
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_regulator_mode(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_mode(component, mode);
-		wcd_clsh_v3_force_iq_ctl(component, mode, true);
+		/*
+		 * Only the first headphone channel runs the start-up IQ sequence:
+		 * its buck and flyback enables put CLASSH_MODE_2/3 and
+		 * FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2 back to their playback values, but for
+		 * the second channel they are already on and skip that, so forcing
+		 * the start-up values again would leave them in place.
+		 */
+		if (!ctrl->buck_users && !ctrl->flyback_users)
+			wcd_clsh_v3_force_iq_ctl(component, mode, true);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_flyback_ctrl(component, ctrl, mode, true);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_current(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_mode(component, mode);
@@ -637,7 +645,15 @@ static void wcd_clsh_v3_state_hph_l(struct wcd_clsh_ctrl *ctrl, int req_state,
 	if (is_enable) {
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_regulator_mode(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_mode(component, mode);
-		wcd_clsh_v3_force_iq_ctl(component, mode, true);
+		/*
+		 * Only the first headphone channel runs the start-up IQ sequence:
+		 * its buck and flyback enables put CLASSH_MODE_2/3 and
+		 * FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2 back to their playback values, but for
+		 * the second channel they are already on and skip that, so forcing
+		 * the start-up values again would leave them in place.
+		 */
+		if (!ctrl->buck_users && !ctrl->flyback_users)
+			wcd_clsh_v3_force_iq_ctl(component, mode, true);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_flyback_ctrl(component, ctrl, mode, true);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_current(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_mode(component, mode);
